["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Most bad days in the bush start small: a wrong turn, wet socks, dark at 6 pm. A plan and a few tools keep them small.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Lost? STOP</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"STOP, step S: Stop. Sit down on a log. Do not keep walking. Most people make it worse by pushing on.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect y=\"220\" width=\"400\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".35\"><polygon points=\"20,220 40,140 60,220\"/><polygon points=\"340,220 360,130 380,220\"/><polygon points=\"300,220 316,160 332,220\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"54\" cy=\"54\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"40\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">S</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"24\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Stop</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Sit down. Do not keep walking.</text>\n  <rect x=\"160\" y=\"196\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"140\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"154\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M200 192 L226 196 L230 220\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pushing on makes it worse</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Stop. Sit down. Do not keep walking.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"STOP, step T: Think. Where did you last know where you were? Picture the truck, the trail, the creek you crossed.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect y=\"220\" width=\"400\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".35\"><polygon points=\"20,220 40,140 60,220\"/><polygon points=\"340,220 360,130 380,220\"/><polygon points=\"300,220 316,160 332,220\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"54\" cy=\"54\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"40\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"24\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Think</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Where did you last know where you were?</text>\n  <rect x=\"160\" y=\"196\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"140\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"154\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M200 192 L226 196 L230 220\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8\" fill=\"none\"/><g fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"122\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"246\" cy=\"108\" r=\"8\"/><ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"120\" rx=\"64\" ry=\"34\"/></g><rect x=\"270\" y=\"112\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><circle cx=\"278\" cy=\"132\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"302\" cy=\"132\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The truck?</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Think. Where did you last know where you were?</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"STOP, step O: Observe. Check your map app and compass, the sun, creeks, and listen for a road.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect y=\"220\" width=\"400\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".35\"><polygon points=\"20,220 40,140 60,220\"/><polygon points=\"340,220 360,130 380,220\"/><polygon points=\"300,220 316,160 332,220\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"54\" cy=\"54\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"40\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">O</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"24\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Observe</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Map, compass, sun, creeks, roads</text>\n  <rect x=\"160\" y=\"196\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"140\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"154\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M200 192 L226 196 L230 220\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8\" fill=\"none\"/><rect x=\"90\" y=\"120\" width=\"40\" height=\"64\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"95\" y=\"128\" width=\"30\" height=\"46\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"150\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"150\" r=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M300 132 l6 18 h-12 Z\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><circle cx=\"340\" cy=\"100\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#e8b10c\"/><path d=\"M250 240 q30 -10 60 0 t60 0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"/>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Observe. Map, compass, sun, creeks, roads.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"STOP, step P: Plan. Stay put, or move only if you are sure. Build shelter and a fire before dark.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect y=\"220\" width=\"400\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".35\"><polygon points=\"20,220 40,140 60,220\"/><polygon points=\"340,220 360,130 380,220\"/><polygon points=\"300,220 316,160 332,220\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"54\" cy=\"54\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"40\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"24\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Plan</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Stay put, or move only if sure</text>\n  <rect x=\"160\" y=\"196\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"140\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"154\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M200 192 L226 196 L230 220\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M270 216 L310 160 L350 216 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M120 216 q-12 -20 0 -40 q4 14 10 16 q6 10 -10 24 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shelter and fire before dark</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Plan. Stay put, or move only if sure.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>STOP: Stop, Think, Observe, Plan (AdventureSmart) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Lost, disoriented or hurt <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the details</summary><ul><li>AdventureSmart teaches STOP: Stop, Think, Observe, Plan <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Some AdventureSmart material uses Sit instead of Stop. Same idea <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Stop:</strong> do not keep walking. Most people make it worse by pushing on.</li><li><strong>Think:</strong> where did you last know where you were?</li><li><strong>Observe:</strong> map app, compass, sun, creeks, the sound of a road.</li><li><strong>Plan:</strong> stay put, or move only if you are sure. Shelter and fire before dark.</li><li>Use it when lost, disoriented or hurt <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2eVVkHfqh0U\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>Hug-A-Tree &amp; Survive film</b><small>Lost? Stop. Stay put. Shelter and signal.<br>AdventureSmart, YouTube, 12 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Trip plan card to leave with someone at home: who is going, vehicle and plate, where you park, your route by car, ATV and boat, the time you will be back, and the time to call 911 if you are not.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"16\" width=\"320\" height=\"270\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"16\" width=\"320\" height=\"40\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"43\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Trip plan</text>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <text x=\"56\" y=\"84\" font-weight=\"bold\">Who:</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"114\" font-weight=\"bold\">Vehicle, plate:</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"144\" font-weight=\"bold\">Parked at:</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"174\" font-weight=\"bold\">Route:</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"174\" font-size=\"14\">car, ATV, boat</text>\n    <text x=\"56\" y=\"210\" font-weight=\"bold\">Back by:</text>\n    <text x=\"56\" y=\"246\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Call 911 if not</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"266\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">back by:</text>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"86\"/><line x1=\"176\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"116\"/><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"146\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"214\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"214\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"270\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"196\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M300 196 v-10 M300 196 h8\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Always leave a trip plan with someone at home <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. List the car, the <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"ATV\">ATV</button> and the boat.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the 3 Ts and the app</summary><ul><li>AdventureSmart's 3 Ts: Trip planning, Training, Taking the essentials <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Always fill out a trip plan and leave it with someone at home <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>AdventureSmart has a free trip plan app that sends your plan to a contact <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Write: who, vehicle and plate, where you park, route, return time, when to call for help.</li><li>Say who to call if you are late: 911, and police will start a search (Tip: confirm with your local police).</li><li>Assumption: you hunt from the car, the ATV and the boat. List all three in the plan.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"bs-tripplan\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"bs-tripplan:0\"><span>Trip plan written and sent</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"bs-tripplan:1\"><span>Return time and \"call 911 if not back by\" time set</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"bs-tripplan:2\"><span>Map of the area downloaded for offline use</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"bs-tripplan:3\"><span>Phone and satellite device charged</span></label></div>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Satellite SOS needs open sky. Under trees, hills or in a canyon it is slow or blocked. Step into a clearing or onto a ridge with a clear view of the sky.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Satellite SOS needs open sky</text>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"58\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"54\" width=\"14\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><rect x=\"210\" y=\"54\" width=\"14\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <rect y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"40,230 70,110 100,230\"/><polygon points=\"80,230 110,100 140,230\"/><polygon points=\"120,230 150,120 180,230\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"222\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <path d=\"M190 68 L120 200\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/>\n  <path d=\"M100 160 l20 20 M120 160 l-20 20\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"310\" cy=\"222\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <path d=\"M210 68 L306 212\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M320 160 l8 10 l16 -20\" stroke=\"#2f6b3a\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"110\" y=\"258\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Under trees ✗</text><text x=\"310\" y=\"258\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">Clearing ✓</text></g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">iPhone 14 or later, or a satellite messenger</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>iPhone 14 or later: Emergency SOS via satellite in Canada, iOS 16.1 or later <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Needs open sky <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: iPhone details and messengers</summary><ul><li>Much of the backcountry near Sun Peaks has no cell signal (Assumption: check with your carrier map).</li><li>iPhone 14 or later can send Emergency SOS via satellite in Canada with iOS 16.1 or later <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Messages via satellite and Find My via satellite also work in Canada on iPhone 14 or later <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Apple says it is free for two years from activation of the phone <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. After that: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li>It needs open sky. Trees, hills and canyons slow or block it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>A dedicated satellite messenger (two way texting and SOS) works on any phone. Needs a paid plan.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>Both carry iPhone 14 or later? That covers SOS. If not, buy or rent a satellite messenger so each hunter can call for help alone.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hypothermia getting worse. Mild: shivering and the umbles, fumbles, mumbles, stumbles, grumbles. Moderate: violent shivering, confusion, poor judgment. Severe: shivering stops, stiff muscles, glassy stare, slow breathing. Emergency.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hypothermia: know the signs</text>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"26\" height=\"230\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"60\" width=\"16\" height=\"205\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"33\" cy=\"268\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <rect x=\"64\" y=\"40\" width=\"326\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8b10c\" fill-opacity=\".3\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"64\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mild</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"84\">Shivering. The \"umbles\":</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"14\">fumbles, mumbles, stumbles, grumbles</text>\n    <rect x=\"64\" y=\"118\" width=\"326\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\".3\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"142\" font-weight=\"bold\">Moderate</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"164\">Violent shivering, confusion</text>\n    <rect x=\"64\" y=\"190\" width=\"326\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"214\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">Severe: EMERGENCY</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"236\" fill=\"#fff\">Shivering STOPS, stiff, glassy</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"256\" fill=\"#fff\">stare, slow breathing</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Out of wind and wet, dry layers, rewarm gently</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Shivering that <strong>stops</strong> is an emergency <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: first aid and October risk</summary><ul><li>Mild: shivering, cold, and the \"umbles\": fumbles, mumbles, stumbles, grumbles <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Moderate: violent shivering, confusion, poor judgment <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Severe: shivering <strong>stops</strong>, stiff muscles, glassy stare, slow breathing. This is an emergency <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>First aid: out of wind and wet, dry layers on, cover head and neck, rewarm gently <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Warm sweet drinks only if fully awake and able to swallow (Tip, common first aid advice).</li><li>October risk: wet from sweat or rain, then sitting still glassing as the sun drops.</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YjjSeiXwEbI\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>How to spot and treat hypothermia</b><small>Spot hypothermia early: shivering, fumbling, confusion.<br>Canadian Red Cross / Croix-Rouge canadienne, YouTube, 1 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Daylight bar for an October afternoon. Turn back time is 1 hour before sunset. Pack a dry layer and a toque. Check fire rules on the BC Wildfire Service app. Report a wildfire at 1 800 663 5555, or star 5555 on a cell.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Leave an hour before dark</text>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"60\" width=\"360\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8b10c\" opacity=\".5\"/>\n  <rect x=\"300\" y=\"60\" width=\"80\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"220\" y=\"60\" width=\"80\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"100\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#e8b10c\"/><rect x=\"280\" y=\"100\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"86\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Hunt</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"86\" fill=\"#fff\">Walk out</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"86\" fill=\"#fff\">Dark</text></g>\n  <path d=\"M220 104 v20\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Turn back</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sunset</text>\n  <path d=\"M232 112 h56\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 hour</text>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"170\" width=\"360\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#c0392b\" fill-opacity=\".12\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M50 250 q-18 -24 0 -56 q6 20 14 22 q10 16 -14 34 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><text x=\"90\" y=\"200\">Report a wildfire</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"226\" fill=\"#c0392b\">1 800 663 5555</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"250\" fill=\"#c0392b\">*5555 on a cell</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\">Check fire rules before any fire</text></g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Turn back 1 hour before sunset. Dry layer and toque every trip.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: fire rules and the numbers</summary><ul><li>Interior October can go from sun to sleet in an afternoon. Pack a dry layer and a toque every trip.</li><li>Daylight is short. Turn back time = 1 hour before sunset.</li><li>Kamloops Fire Centre campfire and open fire rules changed in late September 2026 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Today's status: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> on the BC Wildfire Service app before any fire.</li><li>Report a wildfire: 1 800 663 5555 toll free, or *5555 on a cell <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Never park a hot vehicle or ATV on dry grass. The exhaust can start a fire (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a bear comes toward you. Aim the spray at the ground a few metres in front of the bear, then sweep up to its face. The orange cloud forms a wall the bear runs into. Never spray into the wind.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bear spray: low, then sweep up</text>\n  <rect y=\"210\" width=\"400\" height=\"90\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"150\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"164\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <line x1=\"52\" y1=\"174\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"78\" y=\"168\" width=\"16\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <g>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"60 0;0 0\" dur=\"5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"320\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"44\" ry=\"28\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><circle cx=\"278\" cy=\"166\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><circle cx=\"272\" cy=\"150\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/>\n    <rect x=\"290\" y=\"196\" width=\"12\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"196\" width=\"12\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#2f2a26\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M96 180 L250 206 L250 160 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;.55;.55\" keyTimes=\"0;0.2;1\" begin=\"1s\" dur=\"3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <animate attributeName=\"d\" values=\"M96 180 L230 214 L230 196 Z;M96 180 L230 214 L230 196 Z;M96 180 L240 200 L240 140 Z\" keyTimes=\"0;0.4;1\" begin=\"1s\" dur=\"3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n  </path>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.1;0.8;1\" begin=\"1s\" dur=\"1.6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Aim at the ground</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.6s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Sweep up to the face</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.5s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"60\" y=\"262\" width=\"280\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"283\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Never spray into the wind</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Aim low, sweep up. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"What to do. Black bear, defensive attack, protecting cubs or food: spray, and if it makes contact play dead. Black bear, predatory attack, stalking you or at night: spray, stand big, fight back. Cougar: never run, look big, back away slowly, if attacked always fight back.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bear or cougar: what to do</text>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <rect x=\"6\" y=\"38\" width=\"388\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n    <text x=\"16\" y=\"62\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bear, defensive</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"14\">cubs or food, surprised</text>\n    <text x=\"210\" y=\"62\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Spray</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"84\">Contact? Play dead</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\">most common type</text>\n    <rect x=\"6\" y=\"124\" width=\"388\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\".2\"/>\n    <text x=\"16\" y=\"148\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bear, predatory</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"14\">stalks you, or at night</text>\n    <text x=\"210\" y=\"148\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Spray</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"170\">Stand big</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"190\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Fight back</text>\n    <rect x=\"6\" y=\"210\" width=\"388\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" fill-opacity=\".2\"/>\n    <text x=\"16\" y=\"234\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cougar</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\">never run</text>\n    <text x=\"210\" y=\"234\">Look big, eye contact</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"254\">Back away slowly</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"274\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Attacked? Fight back</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Spray on the hip belt or chest, not in the pack (Tip).</li></ul>","<details class=\"more\"><summary>More: spray range, grizzlies, and who to call</summary><ul><li>Black bears live around Kamloops and Sun Peaks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Grizzlies: the Thompson Nicola region holds about 317 grizzlies <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. A Sun Peaks visitor site says only black bears at the resort <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>. My lean: carry spray as if both are there.</li><li>Bear spray: point it at the ground a few metres in front of the bear, then sweep up to its face <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Do not spray into the wind. It will blow back on you <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Range: about 3 m to 10 m depending on the can. Read your can <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Black bear attack: defensive (cubs or food) is the most common type. Spray. If it makes contact, play dead (75%, Parks Canada).</li><li>Predatory attack (stalks you, or at night): spray, stand big, fight back. Do not play dead (75%, Parks Canada).</li><li>Cougar: never run, look big, back away slowly, keep eye contact. If attacked, always fight back (75%, WildSafeBC).</li><li>A gut pile draws bears. Move the meat away from it fast and watch your back.</li><li>Report a dangerous bear or cougar: RAPP (Report All Poachers and Polluters) 1 877 952 7277, open 24/7, for wildlife and human conflicts where public safety is at risk (synopsis page 2) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aIvpLzHiCrg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>How to Use Bear Spray - Banff National Park</b><small>Remove the clip, aim low, spray a cloud between you and the bear.<br>Parks Canada, YouTube, 2 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C1Zgewb8oRI\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>How to Use Bear Spray</b><small>One minute bear spray demo.<br>AlbertaParks, YouTube, 1 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Tourniquet on an arm. Use it for life threatening bleeding from a limb when firm pressure fails. Put it a few centimetres above the wound, between the wound and the heart, never on a joint. Tighten until the bleeding stops and write down the time.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tourniquet: where it goes</text>\n  <!-- arm -->\n  <path d=\"M20 120 L180 110 Q 200 108 210 120 L380 126 L380 176 L210 170 Q 200 182 180 180 L20 180 Z\" fill=\"#d9b48f\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Heart side</text>\n  <!-- elbow -->\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"146\" r=\"20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Not on a joint</text>\n  <!-- wound -->\n  <ellipse cx=\"320\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n  <text x=\"340\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wound</text>\n  <!-- tourniquet -->\n  <rect x=\"262\" y=\"120\" width=\"18\" height=\"60\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"250\" y=\"104\" width=\"42\" height=\"10\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <line x1=\"271\" y1=\"114\" x2=\"271\" y2=\"122\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"271\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Above the wound</text>\n  <path d=\"M282 196 L308 196\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M286 190 l-6 6 l6 6 M304 190 l6 6 l-6 6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <!-- clock -->\n  <circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"248\" r=\"24\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M70 248 V232 M70 248 h12\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"104\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Tighten until bleeding stops.</text>\n  <text x=\"104\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Write the time.</text>\n  <text x=\"104\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Firm pressure first</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Firm pressure first. Life threatening limb bleed and pressure fails: tourniquet, 5 to 10 cm (2 to 4 in) above <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: Red Cross steps and the kit</summary><ul><li>The big killer after a fall, knife slip or gunshot is bleeding from an arm or leg.</li><li>Red Cross guidance: firm direct pressure first. If bleeding from a limb is life threatening and pressure fails, use a tourniquet <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Place it about 5 to 10 cm (2 to 4 in) above the wound, between wound and heart. Tighten until bleeding stops. Write the time <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Buy a commercial windlass tourniquet, not a homemade one. The Red Cross training kit uses the SOFTT (Special Operations Forces Tactical Tourniquet) type <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Kit carried by each hunter on the body: tourniquet, gauze, pressure bandage, gloves, emergency blanket, lighter.</li><li>Take a first aid course. A kit you do not know how to use is weight.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Tell someone where you went. Pack like you will sleep out. Leave the bush an hour before dark.</p></aside>","<aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>No trip plan, \"only up the road\".</li><li>Bear spray buried in the pack.</li><li>Sweating on the climb, then sitting still wet.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Fill out the AdventureSmart trip plan. Test SOS demo mode on your iPhone. Practise drawing bear spray in under 2 seconds, safety clip on.</p></aside>","<ul><li>RAPP number read directly in the Synopsis <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Everything else through search previews, capped at 85%.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.adventuresmart.ca/the-three-ts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AdventureSmart: The Three Ts</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://globalnews.ca/news/9437036/b-c-adventure-smart-safety-plan-stop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Global News: BC AdventureSmart safety plan, STOP</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://support.apple.com/en-ca/101573\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Support: Use Emergency SOS via satellite on your iPhone (Canada)</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://support.apple.com/en-us/120930\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apple Support: About Messages via satellite</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://www.redcross.org/take-a-class/resources/learn-first-aid/hypothermia\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Red Cross: hypothermia</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://www.redcross.ca/training-and-certification/first-aid-tips-and-resources/first-aid-tips/cold-related-emergencies-staying-warm-and-safe-in-canadian-winters\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Canadian Red Cross: cold related emergencies</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://www.redcross.org/take-a-class/resources/articles/how-to-apply-a-tourniquet\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Red Cross: how to apply a tourniquet</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/mtn/ours-bears/securite-safety/gaz-spray\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Parks Canada: bear spray, mountain national parks</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/nt/nahanni/securite-safety/ours_bears/security-safety\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Parks Canada: A guide to safety, Nahanni (attack types)</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bcforestsafe.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Safety-Alert-of-the-Month-March-2025-Final.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Forest Safety Council: bear spray safety alert</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://wildsafebc.com/species/cougar/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">WildSafeBC: Cougar</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://tnccollaborative.org/in-our-backyard-grizzly-bear/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Thompson Nicola Conservation Collaborative: In Our Backyard, Grizzly Bear</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bestsunpeaks.com/bears-in-sun-peaks.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Best Sun Peaks: Bears in Sun Peaks</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview, visitor site)</li><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/safety/wildfire-status/contact-channels/report-a-wildfire\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Report a wildfire</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://cfjctoday.com/2026/09/29/category-2-and-3-open-fires-permitted-within-the-cariboo-fire-centre/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Kamloops Fire Centre open fire update, CFJC Today</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview, news)</li><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, read directly: page 2 (RAPP number and what to report). Checked 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li>Note: all other pages read through search previews. Capped at 85%.</li></ul></details>"]